    {
      "id": "claim_55603045000448a7b873bfbbca2d5e07",
      "statement": "ulabase.setup.ts is a declarative setup configuration that defines check/apply steps for configuring Ulabase services.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8da51c063cbd3c47f4512b5380cc8c7a72fbc7527c95ef7c010275f113161874:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_33bf5a4d00a642d68f092911bae86623",
      "statement": "Every setup step is idempotent: its check examines desired state, the apply runs only when the check fails, and `--dry-run` runs the checks only, so re-running against a configured service writes nothing and reports each step satisfied.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L10-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1415b41f8bbb11819a6a907d1c2dc376e2cc75662428cbb11222a5b5109e9e38:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c152187b7014a969c8eb63a34d01c56",
      "statement": "SHOPPERS = ['$unauthenticated', 'user'] is granted as one ACL permission with two roles because the ACL authorizer attaches only the first permission it matches: a guest-only permission would 403 signed-in users, and two rules for the same path would make which one applies depend on role order.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L51-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ab31a227027cb015c45f362ba4f6922a0ef47e092f7f582034614648c8c3f54:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b478e6e691da452b82f097448050dfd7",
      "statement": "Secret handling is variable-wins: `secret(name, stored)` returns `fromEnv(name)` and records the name in the pushed set when the environment variable is set, otherwise it returns the stored value; `wantsReplacing` consults that pushed set so a step whose secret is named in the environment stays unsatisfied until the secret has been written in this run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.ts#L138-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e3f3b538e417861303fa27a5032c055d6a4c8a9190813c49233a48e8995f67b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0abc4801a9be4dcb9350413d5a074acc",
      "statement": "The sample-catalog step writes content, not configuration: its check asks whether the catalog collection holds anything at all (not whether specific demo products are present), and it seeds DEMO_PRODUCTS via upsert only when the catalog is empty, so re-running the setup never overwrites real catalog data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/catalog.seed.ts#L7-L10",
